+# Bench Paste · dual-plane Browser Plugin
+
+Test fixture — **do not publish**. A dual-plane plugin: the host half `index.js` registers the
+lifecycle and keeps no coupling, and the browser half `client.js` adds a 📋 button to the composer
+tool row that reads the LLM provider directory through `ctx.remote` and appends the provider count
+to the draft.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+- **Host mount.** `cordis.patch.yml` inserts the `bench-paste` row, so the package's `index.js`
+  activates in the host tree.
+- **Installable bundle.** `dsh plugin --profile <name> add <this directory>` installs the package
+  and, because the manifest declares `dsh.bundle.patch`, appends it to `dsh.profile.bundles`.
+- **Browser half.** `client.js` registers the 📋 button into the composer tool row through the slot
+  registry — `conversation.input.left`, declared by `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation` — and
+  appends the provider count to the composer draft through the `inputActions.setDraft` standard prop
+  that every session-scope slot receives. It declares the runtime services it waits for with Cordis
+  `inject = ["slots", "remote", "remote.llm"]`; the registration is removed with the plugin fiber.
+- **Browser entry point.** The package is composed into `window.__DSH_BOOT__.entries` by the client
+  module system and its bytes are served from the versioned combo route
+  (`/plugins/??@demo/dsh-bench-paste/client.js&rev=<rev>`); this release has no bare
+  `/plugins/<package>/client.js` route.
+
+## Manifest
+
+The browser declaration lives in the alpha `dsh.client` field:
+
+```json
+"dsh": {
+  "client": {
+    "platform": "web",
+    "inject": ["@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-remotes", "@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation"]
+  },
+  "bundle": { "patch": "./cordis.patch.yml" }
+}
+```
+
+`./client` must be a client-module factory bundle: a classic script that registers one lazy
+closure factory with `window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })`. Executing the script only
+registers the factory; the module body (and therefore the button) runs at materialization, and the
+exported `apply`/`inject` are read by the Cordis Loader from the factory's exports. `react` is a
+shell-seeded platform module, so the factory receives it from the module table's `require`.
+
+Three dependency declarations look alike and none is interchangeable: Cordis `inject` names the
+services the fiber waits for, `dsh.client.external` would name non-baseline module-table requests
+(this plugin has none), and `dsh.client.inject` carries informational package-name edges only.
+
+Every `ctx.remote` call answers with a `{ ok, value }` envelope: `ok: false` carries the
+`RemoteError` instead of a thrown value.
+
+## History
+
+An earlier revision declared the browser half in the top-level `client` field (the 0.1.1
+convention) and exported `apply` as an ES module, so the host half activated while the browser half
+silently never reached `__DSH_BOOT__.entries`. The declaration now lives in `dsh.client`, `./client`
+carries the loader factory contract, and the button writes through the composer's `inputActions`
+instead of a `document.querySelector('textarea')` lookup — the shipped composer is a Lexical
+contenteditable, so the DOM lookup no longer reached the input.
